Hi @<%= @actor.display_login %>,

Your enterprise, <%= @business.name %> that you are <%= @role_and_preposition %>, now requires all users to have secure two-factor authentication (2FA) methods.
You currently have SMS/Text message configured as a 2FA method, which is not considered secure.
To access <%= @business.name %> resources, remove SMS/Text message as a 2FA method.

If this is your only 2FA method, you will need to add an authenticator app as a 2FA method before you can remove SMS/Text message.

After you add an authenticator app, you can add additional secure 2FA methods such as:
- Security keys
- Passkeys
- GitHub Mobile App
<%= link_to "Update your two-factor authentication methods", settings_security_url(:host => GitHub.urls.host_name) %>

